  "content": {
    "title": "Chipotle BOGO burritos and more for showing tattoos. Where to get in Ohio",
    "text": "March 13, 2026, 10:48 a.m. ETHave tattoos? Chipotle is offering a lucky deal for customers with real (or fake) ink on Friday, March 13, but there's a catch — it's only for one hour.The chain's “Tatted Like a Chipotle Bag” promotion plays off the scribble designs on its bags and the flash‑tattoo culture tied to Friday the 13th. The deal is only available in restaurants and not online.Here's what to know.When can you get Chipotle BOGO deal for tattooed customers?According to Chipotle, the BOGO free entrée will be available in Chipotle restaurants in the U.S. and Canada on Friday, March 13, 2026, from 3-4 p.m. local time.The promotion is limited to five free menu items per check and is subject to availability. Each free item requires the purchase of a full‑price entrée of equal or greater value, the chain notes.Does it have to be a real tattoo to claim the deal?No. Chipotle says that all types of tattoos count, including \"real, temporary, freshly Sharpied or any other creative iteration.\"Do customers have to be rewards members to redeem Chipotle's tattoo BOGO deal?No, Chipotle's flash tattoo BOGO deal is open to anyone with ink, real or fake. No membership required.However, Chipotle rewards members who scan in restaurants at checkout will unlock a Friday the 13th \"Tatted Like a Chipotle Bag\" badge in the Chipotle app. Purchased entrées are eligible for Chipotle Rewards points.How many Chipotle restaurants are in Ohio?Ohio has 270 Chipotle locations, including 23 in Cincinnati, 21 in Columbus, six in Akron and four in Canton.The chain also has several Kentucky locations near Cincinnati: Florence (three), Covington (one), Newport (one), Erlanger (one) and Fort Mitchell (one).",
